  <section aria-labelledby="ds-capabilities-title" class="ds-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">Security engineered for builders</div>
        <h2 id="ds-capabilities-title">A clearer path from risk to resolution</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="ds-grid">
        <article class="ds-card"><span class="ds-icon" aria-hidden="true">01</span><h3>Pull request security</h3><p>Diff-aware deterministic checks, risk gates, SARIF findings and optional AI-assisted context before changes merge.</p></article>
        <article class="ds-card"><span class="ds-icon" aria-hidden="true">02</span><h3>API &amp; agent trust</h3><p>Checks for risky authentication boundaries, webhook signatures, overbroad agent authority and insecure integrations.</p></article>
        <article class="ds-card"><span class="ds-icon" aria-hidden="true">03</span><h3>WAAP edge protection</h3><p>Programmable web and API controls including request contracts, GraphQL limits, bot signals and staged observe/block policy.</p></article>
        <article class="ds-card"><span class="ds-icon" aria-hidden="true">04</span><h3>Security intelligence</h3><p>Dependency evidence, repository security graphs, regression tracking and approval-gated remediation proposals.</p></article>
        <article class="ds-card"><span class="ds-icon" aria-hidden="true">05</span><h3>Cloud reporting API</h3><p>A tenant-isolated Cloudflare Worker backend for structured scan ingestion and reporting, with scoped API keys and quotas. Deployment pending.</p></article>
        <article class="ds-card"><span class="ds-icon" aria-hidden="true">06</span><h3>Professional implementation</h3><p>Installation, baseline tuning, policy rollout and ongoing security review for teams that need help getting started.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ds-section ds-alt" aria-labelledby="ds-steps-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head"><div class="eyebrow">Simple developer workflow</div><h2 id="ds-steps-title">Protect every release</h2></div>
      <div class="ds-steps">
        <div><strong>01. Connect</strong><p>Add the DevShield GitHub Action to your CI workflow.</p></div>
        <div><strong>02. Assess</strong><p>Scan changed code and review evidence-linked findings.</p></div>
        <div><strong>03. Improve</strong><p>Prioritize fixes, validate protection and approve changes.</p></div>
        <div><strong>04. Scale</strong><p>Adopt managed reporting and API access as they become available.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="ds-codebox" aria-label="DevShield GitHub Action usage example">
        <span>GitHub Actions / example</span>
        <pre><code>- uses: mabrig1/mabrig-devshield-ai@v1
  with:
    github-token: &#36;{{ github.token }}
    fail-on: high</code></pre>
      </div>
      <p class="ds-note">The open-source Action operates without requiring a commercial subscription.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

